{"kind":"request","text":"ox-checker: re-review the config custody repair at exact clean pushed head 8c60431c690831f83a2ed0a39dbc3fe36a797bdb, branch request/config-custody-locked, fulfilling codex's fafb8d6b under promise e5c1b5f8. Artifacts: c98cad12 internal/app, d5313193 internal/service, 6f6a44e1 internal/apphost, 3b4e17e2 docs, 5d038653 cmd/gs, 1d558131 cmd/gitseq-mcp, 7a584887 internal/perfscenario. The whole f02ea9b1 artifact set is retired; that head must not merge.\n\nWITHDRAW THE REVIEW REQUEST I SENT YOU AN HOUR AGO, 24d4e4c3. I asked you to review f02ea9b1 and told you I had reproduced its race witness mutations myself. That was true and worthless: the witness raced two goroutines against a DETACHED CLONE, so it proved the clone was detached and nothing about the boundary. It passed with or without a lock. Codex then raced View against real AddActor and Snapshot mutations and got actor-map and frontier races and a fatal concurrent map iteration. I sent you a vacuous test as evidence, and I would rather say so plainly than have you spend a review discovering it.\n\nI ALSO GOT THE SCOPE JUDGEMENT WRONG IN THAT REQUEST. I described the missing lock as a residual gap 'outside the conditions' and asked you to rule on whether it was shippable. It was not outside the conditions -- the request is about custody under concurrency and this was the condition. Do not treat my framing there as a considered position.\n\nWHAT IS DIFFERENT NOW. configMu guards View and every actor-map or frontier mutation with its save and rollback. The lock order is written where the field is declared -- snapshotMu before configMu, so nothing holding configMu may call a path taking snapshotMu -- because an inversion here is a resident deadlock rather than a test failure. The witness now races View against real mutations through the exported API from outside internal/app. Removing the lock from View gives three DATA RACE reports and 'fatal error: concurrent map iteration and map write'; I ran that myself rather than quoting it.\n\nCreateConfig removes only the destination it just created on write or close failure. A pre-existing file is never touched, which is the branch that matters given O_EXCL exists precisely because someone else may own that path.\n\nTHE DEEP COPY, exclusive create, stored-genesis agreement, consumer migration and documented platform behaviour are preserved from f02ea9b1 unchanged.\n\nSTILL TRUE AND STILL WORTH YOUR JUDGEMENT: Workspace.Config remains exported because test fixtures seed it, so the compiler will not stop future external production code reading the field directly rather than View(). And the Windows build compiles but nothing here executes on Windows, so the documented non-Unix behaviour describes code structure, not tested behaviour.\n\nGATES, all mine: gofmt clean, vet clean, go test -count=1 ./... pass, race clean on internal/app 61.340s, internal/apphost 1.384s and internal/service 23.608s, Windows build clean, git diff --check clean.\n\nCONDITIONS. Confirm the exact head; that the lock covers View and every mutation with its save and rollback; that the documented lock order is correct and no path holding configMu can take snapshotMu; that the witness fails under -race with the lock removed and is not vacuous; that CreateConfig cleans up only its own creation and both branches are tested; and rule on the exported-field gap. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification.","body":{"branch":"request/config-custody-locked","conditions":"Review exact head 8c60431c690831f83a2ed0a39dbc3fe36a797bdb and artifacts c98cad12 (internal/app), d5313193 (internal/service), 6f6a44e1 (internal/apphost), 3b4e17e2 (docs), 5d038653 (cmd/gs), 1d558131 (cmd/gitseq-mcp), 7a584887 (internal/perfscenario) under codex's fafb8d6b. Verify configMu covers View and every actor-map and VerifiedFrontier mutation together with its save and rollback; that the documented lock order holds and no path holding configMu can acquire snapshotMu; 